   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   = note: a slice whose elements read as `Rendered` in place is `Slice<Erased<Rt, Rendered>, Shared, Rt>` or `Slice<Erased<Rt, Rendered>, Mut, Rt>` (a Rust `&[Erased<Rt, Rendered>]` or `&mut [Erased<Rt, Rendered>]` parameter is the same): each element reads as `&Rendered` by `as_ref(rt)` and as `&mut Rendered` by `as_mut(rt)`, where `Rendered: Stored<Rt>`, as a scalar and an extension type are (RFC-0047).
   = note: a type that is not `Stored`, as a derived struct or enum is not, has no element read in place: a `Vec` of it taken by value materializes each element.
   = help: the following other types implement trait `TransparentOver<Rt>`:
